One of these integers is within 1/2 of the rational number alpha, right, in absolute value? So I can arrange that the remainders lie between -1/2 and 1/2 instead of 0 and 1.

127
00:33:59,070 --> 00:34:09,300
然后 r₀² + s₀² 就——这 ≤ Delta(A) 乘以(1/4 + 1/4)，即 Delta(A) 的 1/2。
And then r_0^2 + s_0^2 is—this is <= Delta(A) times (1/4 + 1/4), which is 1/2 of Delta(A).

128
00:34:09,300 --> 00:34:17,273
我发现我现在必须在这里写 ≤。斯蒂芬妮有问题？
And I see that now I have to put <= here. Yeah, Stephanie?

129
00:34:17,273 --> 00:34:30,177
我倒不在乎开闭端点，但你说得对，应该指明其中一个端点；那就这么办，这样余数就唯一了。尽管这对证明不重要，但这是个好问题。
I couldn't care less, but you're right, you should specify one [endpoint]; let's do it that way, that makes it unique, okay. Although it's not important for this proof, it's a good point.

130
00:34:30,177 --> 00:34:42,328
请注意这多么绝妙。我的意思是，如果我去到不同的环——我接下来要给出不同的环，在那里这套做法将会惨遭失败！
So notice how cool this is. I mean, if I go to different rings—and I'm going to give you different rings where this thing is going to fail miserably!

131
00:34:42,328 --> 00:34:54,047
例如，假设我们不再研究高斯整数（我们刚由该性质证明了它是欧几里得环），而是尝试复数域的一个稍微复杂一点的子环，
So for example, suppose instead of doing the Gaussian integers, which we've just proved are Euclidean by this property, we had tried a slightly more complicated subring of the complex numbers,

132
00:34:54,047 --> 00:35:11,699
即这个环：考虑如下的环，考虑 R，包含所有形如 a + b √(-5) 的元素，该环记作 Z[√(-5)]。
which is this ring: consider the following ring, consider R, all of the things of the form a + b \sqrt{-5}, so that ring would be denoted Z[\sqrt{-5}].

133
00:35:11,699 --> 00:35:14,409
这类似于 Z[√(-1)]，由 a + b 乘以√(-1) 构成。
This is like Z[\sqrt{-1}], a + b times the square root of minus 1.

134
00:35:14,409 --> 00:35:24,159
你在其中通过把 a 和 b 分别相加来进行加法，并通过利用该数的平方等于 -5 的事实来进行乘法。
So you add things here by adding the a's and b's, and you multiply them by just using the fact that this number is a number whose square is -5.

135
00:35:24,159 --> 00:35:29,020
好，现在你可能会说：为什么我们不证明这个环是欧几里得环呢？
Okay, now you might say: well, why don't we prove this ring is Euclidean?

136
00:35:29,020 --> 00:35:42,314
我们可以取 Delta(a +b √(-5)) 为其绝对值的平方，就像对复数做的那样；那将是 a² + 5b²，对吧？
We could take Delta(a + b \sqrt{-5}) to be the square of its absolute value, just like we did for these complex numbers; that would be a^2 + 5b^2, right?

137
00:35:42,314 --> 00:36:08,097
但看看在这里它是如何失效的：即使我们做这个除法——你可以做这个除法，把有理商写成整数加上 -1/2 到 1/2 之间的部分——但到了这里，你得到的不是 Delta(A) 乘以 r₀² + s₀²，而是 r₀² + 5 s₀²。
But look how that fails over here: even when we do this division—and you can do this division, and you write your quotient rational thing as an integer plus something between -1/2 and 1/2—when you go here, you get Delta(A) times not r_0^2 + s_0^2, but r_0^2 + 5 s_0^2.

138
00:36:08,097 --> 00:36:13,209
而 5 乘以 1/4 等于 5/4，两者相加不再小于 1 了！
And 5 times 1/4 is 5/4, and this doesn't add up to a number less than 1 anymore!

139
00:36:13,209 --> 00:36:29,450
所以你在这个环上选取欧几里得大小函数的自然方案失效了，事实上该环不是欧几里得环——至少高斯的证明无法奏效。
So your natural choice for a Euclidean size function on this ring fails, and in fact this ring is not Euclidean—this doesn't work, at least in Gauss's proof.

140
00:36:32,310 --> 00:36:52,135
事实上 R 不是欧几里得环：对任何大小函数你都无法在此环中找到欧几里得算法，更不用说绝对值平方了。
In fact R is not Euclidean: you can't find a Euclidean algorithm in this ring for any size function, let alone the absolute value squared.

141
00:36:52,135 --> 00:36:58,223
原因在于由欧几里得环推导出的性质之一在此失效了。
And the reason is that one of the properties that follows from being Euclidean fails.

142
00:36:58,223 --> 00:37:24,104
特别地，我们最终会看到并非每个理想都是主理想；但我首先要向大家展示的是它不具有唯一分解，因为数 6 在 R 中有两个不同的分解：
In particular, we'll see eventually that not every ideal is principal; but what I'll show you is that you don't have a unique factorization, as the number 6 in R has two distinct factorizations:

143
00:37:24,104 --> 00:37:40,734
即在此环中你可以把 6 写成 2 乘以3——这很容易，在整数中也可以这么做——但你也可以把它写成 (1 + √(-5)) 乘以(1 - √(-5))。
namely, in this ring you can write 6 as 2 times 3—well that's pretty easy, you could do that in the integers too—but you can also write it as (1 + \sqrt{-5}) times (1 - \sqrt{-5}).

144
00:37:40,734 --> 00:37:52,772
事实证明，这四个元素 2、3、1 + √(-5)和 1 - √(-5) 全是该环中的素元。
And it turns out that all four of the elements 2, 3, 1 + \sqrt{-5}, and 1 - \sqrt{-5} are primes in the ring.

145
00:37:52,772 --> 00:38:10,440
我们必须证明这一点，但无论如何，这里的 2——2 在该环中并不整除它；看，如果你尝试用 2 除这个数，你得到的数不在环内：它不是整数加整数乘 √(-5) 的形式，而是 1/2 + 1/2 √(-5)，对吧？
We have to show that, but in any case, this 2— 2 does not divide this in this ring; see, if you try to divide this number by 2, you get something which isn't in the ring: it wouldn't be of the form an integer plus an integer times \sqrt{-5}, it would be 1/2 + 1/2 \sqrt{-5}, right?

146
00:38:10,440 --> 00:38:23,917
所以因为这里有两种不同的因数分解，我们绝不可能拥有上面的任何性质；特别是，这个环中必然存在不是主理想的理想。
So because we have two different factorizations here, we couldn't possibly have any of the properties above; in particular, there have to be ideals in this ring that aren't principal.

147
00:38:23,917 --> 00:38:35,170
事实上，如果你想看一个非主理想的例子：取由 2 和 1 + √(-5) 生成的理想 (2, 1 + √(-5))，它不是主理想。
So in fact, if you want to see an ideal that is not principal: take the ideal generated by 2 and 1 + \sqrt{-5}: (2, 1 + \sqrt{-5}) is not principal.

148
00:38:37,100 --> 00:38:54,805
你会发现 R/I——如果我没记错的话，我真希望我记对了，彼得——同构于 Z/2Z，对吧，它是2 之上的分歧理想！
You'll find that R/I—if I got this right, I sure hope I got this right, Peter—is Z/2Z, yeah right, it's the ramified ideal above 2!

149
00:38:54,805 --> 00:39:11,049
好，这里有一个理想：商环是 Z/2Z，因此它是将a + b √(-5) 映为整数 a + b mod 2 的同态的核。
Okay, so here's an ideal: it turns out the quotient is Z/2Z, and so it's the kernel of the homomorphism that takes a + b \sqrt{-5} to the number a + b mod 2.

150
00:39:11,049 --> 00:39:26,100
所以如果你取这个从 R 到Z/2Z 的映射，你可以验证这是环同态；它的核 I 包含元素 2，并且也包含这个数。
So if you take this homomorphism from R to Z/2Z, you can check that that's a homomorphism of rings; it has a kernel I which contains the number 2, and it also contains this number.

151
00:39:26,100 --> 00:40:00,098
该理想不是主理想，因此一切都不成立了：这里不可能是欧几里得环。有提问？在这里，它们是有理数，但当我把它们乘以这个数 A 时，结果必在环中，原因是：B 在环中，A 与 M也在环中，因此 B - MA 在环中。
That ideal is not principal, and so everything goes wrong: you can't have a Euclidean ring here. Yes? Here, they're rational numbers, but when I multiply them by this number A, they have to be in the ring, and the reason is: B is in the ring, A and M are in the ring, so therefore B - M * A is in the ring.

152
00:40:00,098 --> 00:40:19,189
所以即使这个数本身不在环Z[i] 中——由于包含 r₀ 和 s₀，它在域 Q(i) 中，在分式域中——但如果你把它乘以原始高斯整数 A，你必得到属于该环的元素。
So even though this number itself is not in the ring, the ring Z[i]—it's in the field Q(i) because r_0 and s_0 are there, it's in the quotient field—but if you multiply it by the original Gaussian integer A, you have to get something which is in the ring.

153
00:40:19,189 --> 00:40:28,757
接着我们通过取不在环中的两部分 Delta 的乘积来计算其 Delta，因为我们仍能对任意复数取绝对值，对吧？
And then we calculate its Delta by taking the product of the two Deltas of these things that aren't in the ring, because we can still take the absolute value of any complex number, okay?

154
00:40:28,757 --> 00:40:39,060
这个绝对值函数无论 a 和 b 是否为整数都有定义，并且依然保持乘法性。这明白了吗？
Somehow this absolute value function is defined whether or not a and b are integers, and it's still multiplicative. Does that make sense?

155
00:40:39,060 --> 00:40:43,420
这确实有点精妙，提得好，是的。
It's a little tricky, good point, yeah.

156
00:40:47,990 --> 00:41:04,402
是的，这正是我们所展示的：这个乘积就是我所称的 R，所以 Delta(R) 就是 Delta(A) 乘以这个奇特元素的 Delta；
Yeah, that's exactly what we're showing: this product is what I'm calling R, so Delta(R) is Delta(A) times Delta of this weird element; and this weird element is the thing that has Delta less than 1/2.

157
00:41:04,402 --> 00:41:15,163
而这个奇特元素的 Delta 小于 1/2。它显然不能在环中，因为环上非零元的 Delta 至少为 1。
It obviously can't be in the ring, because Delta on the ring is at least 1, because the complex absolute value is multiplicative.

158
00:41:15,163 --> 00:41:24,816
复数绝对值具有乘法性。看，这是复数域的一个子环，这正是我们在这里使用的奇迹：|z w| = |z| |w|。
See, this is a subring of the complex numbers, and that's the miracle that we're using here, that you know, |z w| = |z| |w|.

159
00:41:24,816 --> 00:41:29,216
如果我们不知道这一点，处理这个函数就会棘手得多。
If we didn't know that, it would be much trickier to work with this function.

160
00:41:29,216 --> 00:41:43,103
好，因此在某些环中我们拥有欧几里得算法，所有这些优美性质都将随之成立；而在某些环中我们没有这些性质，没有欧几里得算法等等。
Okay, so in some rings we're going to have Euclidean algorithms, and all these nice properties are going to follow; and in some rings we're not going to have these properties, and we're not going to have Euclidean algorithm, etc., etc.

161
00:41:43,103 --> 00:41:54,188
接下来你可能会问自己：是否可能证明唯一分解，或者由 (1) 推出的一切？
So the next thing you might ask yourself is: would it be possible to prove unique factorization, or everything following from (1)?

162
00:41:54,188 --> 00:42:05,980
是否可能一个环的每个理想都是主理想，但它却不是欧几里得环？答案是肯定的。
Could it be possible that I could have every ideal principal without it being Euclidean? And the answer is yes.

163
00:42:05,980 --> 00:42:15,355
那么是否也可能拥有唯一分解，但并非每个理想都是主理想？我的意思是，这些性质之间真的存在强弱层级吗？
And is it also possible that I could have unique factorization without every ideal being principal? I mean, are these things actually stronger than each other?

164
00:42:15,355 --> 00:42:20,830
让我们画一个简图，然后我会对我们接下来的走向作些说明。
So let's make a little diagram, and then I'll make some remarks about where we're going.

165
00:42:27,430 --> 00:43:07,021
我们已经证明了：“R 是欧几里得环”蕴涵“R 是所谓的主理想整环”，即每个理想都是主理想，每个理想 I 都是主理想；有时简称为 PID，即主理想整环。
So we've shown: the property 'R is Euclidean' implies the property that R is what's called a principal ideal domain, which means every ideal is principal, every ideal I is principal; sometimes this is called a PID for short, principal ideal domain.

166
00:43:07,021 --> 00:43:27,370
由此进一步推导出具有分解为素元素的唯一分解——我们可能还需要定义什么是素元素——但我们已经有了这些蕴涵关系。
And then from that it follows that you have unique factorization into prime elements—we have to define what prime elements are, possibly—but we have these implications.

167
00:43:27,370 --> 00:43:38,953
我们已经在黑板上列出了几个满足此性质的环：Z、域上的多项式环 F[x] 以及高斯整数环 Z[i]，因此它们具备其余全部性质。
And we've already got several rings up here: Z, polynomials over a field F[x], and the Gaussian integers Z[i], that satisfy this property, and so they have all the others.

168
00:43:38,953 --> 00:43:51,509
好，现在我们要探讨的是：环中可以拥有唯一分解，却不必具备前两条性质。
Okay, now what we're going to explore is the fact that you can have unique factorization in rings without having these two properties.

169
00:43:51,509 --> 00:43:58,717
因此我将给你们一个环的例子，我们将证明它具有唯一分解，但不是主理想整环。
So I'll try to give you an example of a ring which we're going to prove has unique factorization, which is not a principal ideal domain.

170
00:43:58,717 --> 00:44:16,380
让我先非常简要地用理想的语言抽象地讨论一下环中的整除性，然后我再给出一个具有良好分解性质却不满足前两个性质的环的例子。
So let me just talk about what prime elements are very briefly discuss in the abstract what divisibility is in an abstract ring in terms of ideals, and then I'll give you an example of a ring where you have unique factorization, but you don't have either of the first two properties.

171
00:44:24,599 --> 00:44:55,628
让我们从理想的角度重新审视“整除”的含义——用理想重新理解整除、素元等全部术语。首先，a在 R 中整除 b 是什么意思？
So let's rethink what 'divides' means—rethink divides, prime, all of our terminology in terms of ideals. First of all, what does it mean that a divides b in R?

172
00:44:55,628 --> 00:45:11,980
这当且仅当在 R 中 b 是 a 的某个倍数，这等价于说b 属于由 a 生成的主理想 (a)，对吧？
Well, that's if and only if b is some multiple of a in R, which is the same thing as saying that b is in the principal ideal (a), okay?

173
00:45:11,980 --> 00:45:29,309
这等价于说由 b 生成的主理想包含在由 a 生成的主理想中：(b) ⊆ (a)。所以整除可以用主理想的包含关系来表述。
Which is the same thing as saying that the principal ideal generated by b is contained in the principal ideal generated by a: (b) \subseteq (a). So divides we can express in terms of containment of principal ideals.

174
00:45:29,309 --> 00:45:59,806
好，我们说它真整除（真因子），如果 a 与 m 在 R 中都不是单位（其中 b = ma）。
All right, we say it divides it properly, if neither a nor m is a unit in R (where b = ma).

175
00:45:59,806 --> 00:46:19,159
这意味着在包含链中，(b) 真包含于 (a)，而 (a) 真包含于 R：(b) ⊊ (a) ⊊ R。
So what that means is that, in this relation, (b) is properly contained in (a), which is properly contained in R: (b) \subsetneq (a) \subsetneq R.

176
00:46:19,159 --> 00:46:36,441
看，这就是 m 不是单位的陈述，因为两个主理想相等当且仅当两个元素互为倍数。
See, this is the statement that m is not a unit, because two principal ideals are equal if and only if both elements are multiples of each other.

177
00:46:36,441 --> 00:46:46,537
如果 m 是单位，那么 a 也是b 乘以 m⁻¹ 的倍数，这意味着不仅 (b) 包含于 (a)，而且 (a) 也包含于 (b)，从而它们必相等。
If m is a unit, then a is also a multiple of b by m^{-1}, and that would say that not only is (b) contained in (a), but (a) is contained in (b), so they have to be equal.

178
00:46:46,537 --> 00:47:05,790
所以 (b) 真包含于 (a) 对应于 m 不是单位；(a) 真包含于 R 对应于 a 不是单位，即 a 生成的理想不等于 1 生成的理想（全环）。
So the statement that (b) is properly contained in (a) is the statement that m is not a unit; the statement that (a) is properly contained in R is the statement that a is not a unit, so the ideal generated by a is not the same as the ideal generated by 1.

179
00:47:05,790 --> 00:47:11,287
因此整除和真整除可以用理想来表达。
So divisibility and proper divisibility can be expressed in terms of ideals.

180
00:47:11,287 --> 00:47:44,722
最后，我们称 p 为素元——有时也称不可约元，如果是讨论多项式环 R 时——如果它不是单位且没有真因子：p 不是单位，且 p 没有R 中的真因子。
And finally, we say that p is a prime—or sometimes it's said irreducible, if you're talking about polynomials in R—if it's not a unit and it has no proper factor: p is not a unit, and p has no proper factor in R.

181
00:47:44,722 --> 00:47:48,940
这就是我们对素元的定义。
Well, that's our notion of a prime.

182
00:47:48,940 --> 00:48:03,257
现在让我们用理想重新表述：这意味着如果你取由 p 生成的主理想 (p)，它不是单位故不等于 R；但——关键在此——
Now let's re-express that in terms of ideals: that says that if you take the principal ideal (p), it's not a unit, so it's not equal to R; but—and this is the key thing—

183
00:48:03,257 --> 00:48:28,562
不存在介于 (p) 与 R 之间的主理想！它在所有主理想中是极大的：即你无法找到严格包含 (p) 且自身不等于 R 的主理想，因为那将对应 p 的真因子。
there are no principal ideals that sit between (p) and R! It is maximal with respect to principal ideals: namely, you cannot find a factor strictly containing (p) which itself is not equal to R, because that would be a proper factor of p.

184
00:48:28,562 --> 00:48:43,030
所以素元正是那些其生成的主理想是真理想，但你无法在它与 R 之间插入任何更大的主理想的元素。
So it says the prime elements are the ones where the principal ideal they generate is a proper ideal, but you cannot put any larger principal ideal between it and R.

185
00:48:43,030 --> 00:48:59,225
好。现在如果我们的环是 PID，从而每个理想都是主理想，这就意味着主理想 (p) 是极大理想！
Okay. Now if our ring is a PID, so that every ideal is principal, this is the statement that the principal ideal (p) is maximal!

186
00:48:59,225 --> 00:49:17,664
因此若 R 是PID，那么 p 是素元当且仅当 (p) 是 R 的极大理想。
So if R is a PID, then p is prime if and only if the ideal generated by p is a maximal ideal of R.

187
00:49:17,664 --> 00:49:35,683
因为介于 (p)与 R 之间的任何理想都必须是主理想——所有理想皆为主理想——而我们已知 (p) 在主理想中是极大的！这等价于说R/(p) 是一个域。
Because any ideal between (p) and R would have to be principal—all ideals are principal—and we know (p) is maximal with respect to principal ideals! And that's the same thing as saying that R/(p) is a field.

188
00:49:35,683 --> 00:49:41,936
记住我们说过可以通过商环来判断极大理想。
Remember we said that we could tell what maximal ideals were by the quotient.

189
00:49:41,936 --> 00:49:52,132
所以我们有了PID 中素元的刻画：当模去其主理想时商环是一个域的元素。
So we have a notion of what a prime is in a PID: it's the elements such that when you quotient out by their principal ideal, it's a field.

190
00:49:52,132 --> 00:50:19,815
现在我断言，在一般环中素元等价于 R/(p) 是整环。对吧？因为如果 p 有真分解 p = mq，且 m与 q 都不是单位或被 p 整除，
Now I claim that a general prime element just means: this is equivalent to R/(p) being an integral domain. Right? Because if I had a proper factorization of p, p = m * q, with neither m nor q units or divisible by p,

191
00:50:19,815 --> 00:50:35,885
那么在该商环中我就会得到乘积为 0，即 mq = 0，由于是整环，这必迫使 m 或 q 为 0，这意味着要么 m 是单位，要么 q是单位。
then in this quotient ring I would have a product that was 0, namely m * q = 0, and that would force either m or q to be 0 because it's an integral domain, which would say that either m was a unit or q is a unit.

192
00:50:35,885 --> 00:50:51,080
所以在一般的环中，如果模去该主理想的商环是整环，你就能判定它是素元；而如果每个理想都是主理想，那么商环就必须是一个域，明白吗。
So in a general ring, you can tell whether you have a prime element if the quotient by that principal ideal is an integral domain; if every ideal is principal, then the quotient by that has to be a field, okay.

193
00:50:51,080 --> 00:51:11,320
现在这为我提供了一种展示“某些环不是主理想整环”的方法：如果我能写出一个元素，使得模去其主理想的商环是整环但不是域，那么必定存在其他理想。好的，我现在就做给你们看。
Now that gives me a way of showing that there are rings that are not principal ideal domains: if I can write down elements where the quotient by that principal ideal is an integral domain which is not a field, then I must have other ideals. Okay, so I'm going to do that for you.

194
00:51:11,320 --> 00:51:40,929
这是一个优美的环的例子，我们将证明它具有唯一分解和漂亮的素元理论，但它不是主理想整环：非 PID 的例子。我们取环 R 为整数上的一元多项式环 Z[x]。
Here's an example of a nice ring where we're going to show has unique factorization, a nice theory of primes, but which is not a principal ideal domain: example of a non-PID. We take the ring R to be polynomials in a variable over the integers, Z[x].

195
00:51:40,929 --> 00:52:01,509
现在取理想 I 为由 x 生成的主理想 (x)。这是一个素元：你无法分解 x；我的意思是它必须是更低次数的多项式，而若次数比它低，那就只能是常数了，对吧？
Now take the ideal I to be the principal ideal generated by x: (x). Now this is a prime element: you can't factor x; I mean it would have to be a polynomial of lesser degree, and if it was of lesser degree, it would be a constant, right?

196
00:52:01,509 --> 00:52:14,139
所以这是——事实上 R/I 同构于整数环 Z（正如大家在考试中证明过的），同态映射将 f(x) 映为 f(0)。
So this is—and in fact R/I is isomorphic, as you showed on the exam, to Z, by the map that takes f(x) to f(0).

197
00:52:14,139 --> 00:52:29,474
而 Z 是整环，这表明 x 在 R 中是素元，因为商环是整环。
And this is an integral domain, so that shows that x is prime in R because the quotient is an integral domain.

198
00:52:29,474 --> 00:52:36,779
但这同时也表明 R 不是主理想整环，因为 Z 不是一个域！
But it also shows that this is not a principal ideal domain, because Z is not a field!

199
00:52:39,729 --> 00:53:00,744
因此，(x) 不可能是 R 的极大理想。也就是说，它在主理想中是极大的，但 R 中存在严格包含它的理想；只不过那些不是主理想。
And consequently, this cannot be a maximal ideal of R. Namely, it's maximal for being a principal ideal, but there are ideals that contain it in R; it's just that they're not principal ideals.

200
00:53:00,744 --> 00:53:20,997
因为既然 Z 不是域，它自身就拥有非平凡理想理论；通过从 Z 中拉回一个非平凡理想，例如理想 2Z——我们可以拉回该理想并得到理想 J，比如由 x 和 2 生成的理想 (x, 2)，其中 R/J恰是 Z/2Z。
Because since this is not a field, it'll itself have ideal theory; and by pulling back a non-trivial ideal from this—for example, the ideal (2Z)—we can pull back that ideal and take this ideal J, say generated by x and 2: (x, 2), where R/J is just Z/2Z.

201
00:53:20,997 --> 00:53:36,958
即从 R 到 R/J 的同态只是将多项式 f 映为 f(0) mod 2。这是一个比 I 更大的理想。
Namely, the homomorphism from R to R/J just takes a polynomial f to f(0) taken mod 2. That's a bigger ideal than I.

202
00:53:36,958 --> 00:53:45,586
但关键在于它不是主理想，因为如果它是主理想，(x) 就不会是素元等等。
But the point is that it's not a principal ideal, because if it were a principal ideal, (x) wouldn't be prime, etc.

203
00:53:45,586 --> 00:54:02,320
所以在这里，因为我们知道一般情况下商环只是整环，而在主理想整环的情形下商环必须是域：只要我们能找到一个理想使得模去该主理想的商环是整环但非域，那么这个环就不是 PID。
So here, because we know that in general it's a domain, whereas in the case of a principal ideal domain the quotient has to be a field: if we can ever find an ideal such that the quotient by that principal ideal is a domain which is not a field, then this thing is not a PID, okay.

204
00:54:02,320 --> 00:54:16,592
好的，但下节课我们将证明性质 (4) 对它依然成立：即我们依然能够证明在这个环中具有素元的唯一分解，尽管它不是欧几里得环，且并非每个理想都是主理想！
But next time we're going to show that property (4) still holds for it: namely, we still are going to be able to prove unique factorization into primes in this ring, even though it's not Euclidean and not every ideal is principal!

205
00:54:16,592 --> 00:54:18,615
我们依然拥有优美的因式分解理论。
We're still going to have a nice theory of factorization.

206
00:54:18,615 --> 00:54:30,328
所以下节课，我们将花大量时间讨论整系数多项式环，这可能是所有环中最引人入胜的一个环。那么下节课见。
So next time, we're going to spend a lot of time on polynomials over the integers, which may be the most interesting ring of them all. So see you then.
